==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Boomerang Cat''' at Level 10.

Evolves into '''Fried Chicken Cat''' when obtained from [[Professional Babbler (Merciless)]] (guaranteed to drop) and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Although you may be excited about his Curse ability with a dash of Long Distance, Bakery Cat is very situational. He can only be particularly useful for stages with [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Aliens]], where he can prevent Warping, and the few [[:Category:Enemies with Toxic ability|Toxic enemies]] he can Curse. He can be stacked, though that doesn't fix his low survivability.

Bakery Cat should not be used against most [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angels]] and [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]] as said enemies often boast extreme stats, abilities such as Curse doesn't do much against them. It certainly doesn't help that they tend to be close-quarters pushers, and Zombies may even catch him if they surface at the wrong time.

He does well in [[Saintly Sister (Merciless)|Papuu's Paradise]], where he can Curse [[Heavenly Herald Papuu|Papuu]] provided you have significant Move Speed Up [[Cat Combo|Combos]], a high-level [[Ototo Corps#Curseblast|Curseblast]], or very good timing skills.

Although Bakery Cat is situational, he can really shine in stages that rely on a single boss in the frontline with an ability that he can remove.

==='''True Form'''===
In its True Form, Fried Chicken Cat is granted Area Attack, improved HP and increased range, which fix a lot of its existing problems. The health boost is good in general, but Area Attacks grant it many more consistent matchups at range, allowing it to safely engage and curse hordes of enemy units. Its role as a {{4c}} ranger isn't in high demand, but it does see use when stacked to snipe enemies at a distance. Curse Immunity and Relic Target are equally important, as many Relics are vulnerable to curse, and tend to be reliant on various status effects, including their own Curse effect. While this unit can't be expected to survive their attacks, it retains its utility in stages with mixed threats, especially those within its other targeted traits and the Relic Doge Base.

The Zombie Killer ability is a good ability to ensure that Zombies this unit curses don't get turned into corpses and to solidify a better usage as a midranger for zombies in {{4c}} stages. Overall, this unit becomes a competent Crowd-Controller and Midranger with Long-Distance attacks.

{{Job|Classification = Crowd-Controller & Midranger}}

